WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.410
Reflective practice helps people learn from experience by examining actions, assumptions,

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.480
evidence, outcomes, and future adjustments.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.995
It is structured, specific, and connected to changed behavior.

00:00:10.995 --> 00:00:12.200
Experience supplies the material,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.075
but reflection turns that material into better questions, better decisions, better tools,

00:00:17.075 --> 00:00:18.160
and better habits.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.400
Strong reflection happens before, during, and after action.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.160
Before action, it clarifies goals, assumptions, risks, and expectations.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.880
During action, it helps people notice confusion and changing conditions.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.480
After action, it reviews what happened and what should change.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:31.985
Together,

00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:36.040
these moments create a learning loop that supports action instead of delaying it.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.545
Evidence and feedback keep reflection honest.

00:00:37.545 --> 00:00:40.565
Facts, artifacts, metrics, peer input, user outcomes,

00:00:40.565 --> 00:00:44.100
and system behavior help separate what happened from what we think it means.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.255
Calibration improves when confidence is updated by evidence.

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:50.800
Hindsight bias is reduced when people ask what was knowable at the time,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.600
not only what seems obvious afterward.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.400
The goal is not endless introspection.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.920
The goal is better judgment, better learning, better systems,

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.160
and more reliable performance over time.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.860
Reflective practice works best when it produces reusable notes, clearer decisions,

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.085
stronger routines, improved team processes,

00:01:05.085 --> 00:01:08.600
and specific adjustments that make the next attempt better than the last.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.585
Used this way, reflection becomes a quiet engineering habit: short enough to sustain,

00:01:12.585 --> 00:01:16.040
honest enough to matter, and practical enough to change what happens next.
